# Makes a character from where render_screens_boot.b3t leaves Rock Band 3
# Deluxe (the welcome hint, on a fresh profile) and shows its portrait: the
# picture in the overshell's Characters list, beside the character's name.
# Creating it (Create, Yes) has RB3 draw the character into a 256x512 render
# target (portrait.tex) and copy that to the character's own portrait texture
# on the CPU (TourChar::CachePortraitTex: DxTex::LockBitmap on the target,
# SetBitmap on the portrait). LockBitmap untiles guest memory's copy of the
# target, which only a resolve fills: under --renderer=native nothing does,
# and src/Hooks/bitmap_readback.cpp draws the target again on the CPU from
# its recorded passes into the bitmap (the log's "Target readback:" line,
# with the time it took); under --renderer=emulated it turns the SDK's
# readback on while the portrait is drawn, so the game copies the emulated
# GPU's own picture. Leaving the closet (Customize Character) takes a
# portrait the same way. Session musicians (prefabs) show a placeholder
# silhouette in the list instead.
#   python tools/band3ctl.py launch --fresh -- --renderer=native --test_random_seed=21 --async_shader_compilation=false
#   python tools/band3ctl.py run tests/game/render_screens_boot.b3t
#   python tools/band3ctl.py window offscreen
#   python tools/band3ctl.py run tests/game/character_portrait.b3t
# The reference is --renderer=emulated --readback_resolve=full, where the
# emulated GPU resolves the target into guest memory and the game's own
# untile reads it. The character is random (its looks aren't seeded), so
# compare a run's portrait-chars against portrait-creator, or the same
# character's portrait across runs through the bitmap itself.
# `window offscreen` first: naming the character opens the SDK's name dialog
# (an overlay, which only takes keys while the window paints), and
# `type {enter}` accepts the name it offers.
# Screenshots are under screenshots/ next to the exe. portrait-create's
# present_stats reply has the game's frame times while the portrait is
# taken. It leaves the game on the main menu.

# the welcome hint: Continue, to the main menu
wait screen=hint_rb3_welcome_screen timeout=30s
sleep 1s
press down
sleep 333ms
press green until screen=main_hub_screen timeout=30s
sleep 2s

# Customize, Create Character: the camera comes in through the barbershop's
# doors first, for about 10 s
press down
sleep 333ms
press down
sleep 333ms
press down
sleep 500ms
press green
sleep 1s
press down
sleep 333ms
press down
sleep 500ms
press green until screen=charactercreator_screen timeout=60s
wait frames=600
# Name: the SDK's dialog, with a name filled in; Enter takes it
press green
sleep 2s
type {enter}
sleep 1500ms
screenshot portrait-creator
# Create, the last of six, then Yes on its question
press down
sleep 333ms
press down
sleep 333ms
press down
sleep 333ms
press down
sleep 333ms
press down
sleep 500ms
press green until screen=charactercreator_create_screen timeout=20s
sleep 1500ms
press up
sleep 400ms
present_stats reset
press green
# the first goal (making a character) is done: its hint, then the main menu
wait screen=hint_goalcomplete_screen timeout=60s
sleep 1s
present_stats
press green until screen=main_hub_screen timeout=60s
sleep 2s

# the overshell's menu (Start), Characters: the new character first, its
# portrait above the list
press start
sleep 1500ms
press down
sleep 400ms
press down
sleep 400ms
press green
sleep 2500ms
screenshot portrait-chars
# back out of the list and the menu
press red
sleep 1s
press red
sleep 1s
